<div class="content-container">

  <div class="jumbotron">
    <h1>Awards<br />
    </h1>
  </div>

    The HAMER organizing committee will award two prizes for the best research presentations at 
    the event: one for the best oral presentation, and one for the best poster presentation.
    <br><br>
    Each prize will cover round-trip airfare for the award recipient to visit an academic or 
    research institution in Greece! These awards are sponsored by Leta Serafim in honor of the 
    memory of her husband Philip Serafim, professor at Northeastern University and National Technical University of Athens.
    <br><br>
    Please refer below for the evaluation criteria used for each presentation format.

    <br><br>

  <table class="table table-bordered table-hover table-condensed">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th style="width:20%;">Evaluation Criterion</th>
        <th style="width:40%;">Oral Presentation</th>
        <th style="width:40%;">Poster Presentation</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Delivery</strong></td>
        <td colspan="2">Was the presentation delivered smoothly, with a clear message that was retained by experts and non-experts in the audience?</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Organization</strong></td>
        <td colspan="2">Did the presentation have a logical organization?</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Visual Aids</strong></td>
        <td>Were slides (text, plots, and other media) used well in conveying information?</td>
        <td>
        <ul>
            <li> Did the poster have a good balance of text and graphics?</li>
            <li> Were the contents of the poster able to convey the overall message by themselves?</li>
        <ul>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Mastery of Subject</strong></td>
        <td colspan="2">Did the presenter demonstrate good knowledge of the subject?</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Results</strong></td>
        <td colspan="2">Did the author present the results clearly and in sufficient detail?</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Innovation</strong></td>
        <td colspan="2">Did the author present any innovative results?</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Time</strong></td>
        <td>Did the speaker stay within the 12-minute limit for the presentation, leaving 3 minutes for audience questions?</td>
        <td>
        <ul>
            <li>Was the speaker's use of the poster space optimal (informative but not crowded)?</li>
            <li>Was the speaker's topic explanation effective and succinct?</li>
        </ul>
        </td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

</div>
